.vercel
.DS_Store
node_modules
*.log

# internal source document - do not publish
*.docx
*.doc
decision-tree-prompt.md

# The horizon photograph used to be ignored, on the reasoning that it was a
# local choice rather than something the repo ships. It is a deliberate part
# of the design now, so it has to be committed — an ignored file is not on the
# deployment, and the page would show the plain page colour there while
# looking right on the machine that chose it.

# secrets and local database settings. Every .env.* is a secret except the
# example, which documents the names and holds no values — `vercel env pull`
# and friends write .env.production and the like, which must never be added.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# a crash dump from a Windows grep, not part of the project
*.stackdump

# a local development database, made by npm run dev:local
.pglite
